OL,3,GNEWSARare birds breed 'furthest north
OL,4,Ain 70 years'
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of Britain's rarest and loudest
OL,7,Fbirds is thought to have bred at a
OL,8,Fnature reserve, believed to be the
OL,9,Ffurthest north in 70 years.
OL,11,FBitterns have bred at Gosforth Nature
OL,12,FReserve, the Natural History Society of
OL,13,FNorthumbria (NHSN) said, with
OL,14,Fhistorical records showing the last
OL,15,Fsigns of breeding were at the site in
OL,16,F1956.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,396,390,260,160,0,100
